#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063929 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064267 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68635d27-a9ef-541b-a57b-d9f5f422ae85" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ac676612-cbb2-5057-a515-501e03414b5a" :question/math-academy-id "e-118" :question/problem "A curve is defined as $y = 2x^2.$ Find the average rate of change of $y$ over the interval $[0,5].$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2x^2.$ Applying the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(0)}{5-(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2(5)^{2})-(2(0)^{2})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{5} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063930 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d13310c-2b80-5945-ada3-31d886f1ec48" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "484ff19c-9a37-553c-a5d5-837a50574703" :question/math-academy-id "e-120" :question/problem "Dave plants a tree in his garden. After $x$ months the tree is $2\\sqrt x + 1$ feet high. What is the average rate of growth of the tree over the first six months?" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}+1$ be the height of the tree after $x$ months. The average rate of growth of the tree over the first six months is the average value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[0,6].$\n\nApplying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(6)-f(0)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}+1-(2\\sqrt{0}+1)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average rate of growth is $\\dfrac {\\sqrt 6} 3 \\approx 0.82$ feet per month."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063931 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f7224e3-9c13-51e7-a3f7-0e379f63a861" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change Given a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "40bfeecc-aa0f-5901-9d75-bc94421b14ec" :question/math-academy-id "e-121" :question/problem "Find the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-1,2]$ given the following table of values for $f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2)-f(-1)}{2-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-(-3)}{2-(-1)} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063932 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051b5337-7671-599f-a7f3-c3fb064575cc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Interval Over Which the Average Rate of Change is Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "50e4be08-7e9b-501b-beae-686aa62e96f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-122" :question/problem "Find the interval where the average rate of change of $f(x)$ equals $0$ given the following table of values for $f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,5\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ | $\\,-5\\,$ | $\\,-7\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{\\Delta f}{\\Delta x}=0$ if and only if $\\Delta f = 0.$ So\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & Δf=0 \\\\  & f(b)-f(a)=0 \\\\  & f(b)=f(a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means we have to find an interval $[a,b]$ such that $f(a)=f(b).$ \n\nSince $f(-2)=f(5)=2,$ we conclude that $\\dfrac{\\Delta f}{\\Delta x}=0$ on the interval $[-2,5].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051b5337-7671-599f-a7f3-c3fb064575cc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Interval Over Which the Average Rate of Change is Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0339a58c-3269-56a1-ab70-ab07f7b79fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-4,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527312} {:answer/id #uuid "75a729a4-326a-505b-b79a-3a7b0fa7f7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-6,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527528} {:answer/id #uuid "9653b005-1544-59c9-8e95-63680d44e093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no such interval" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527607} {:answer/id #uuid "9e090bee-c540-5647-901e-82ff86cf33a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-2,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527632} {:answer/id #uuid "d90910a5-31a5-5178-a05d-bf56be7e06bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0339a58c-3269-56a1-ab70-ab07f7b79fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-4,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527312} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d8445b-24ed-5fc0-a9d0-08fdb9824b20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5d8a95f-b00e-51c0-82a6-3182a1f44e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-101739" :question/problem "Find the interval where the average rate of change of $f(x)$ equals $0$ given the following table of values of $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-6\\,$ | $\\,-4\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,-7\\,$ | $\\,-5\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,5\\,$ | $\\,-5\\,$ | $\\,-8\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ if and only if $Δf=0.$ So\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & Δf=0 \\\\  & f(b)-f(a)=0 \\\\  & f(b)=f(a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means we have to find an interval  $[a,b]$ such that $f(a)=f(b).$\n\nSince $f(-4)=f(4)=-5,$ we conclude that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ on the interval $[-4,4].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f7224e3-9c13-51e7-a3f7-0e379f63a861" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change Given a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a3ab933-6930-5f67-8ca1-c0039736f563" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527401} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd985ef-5d53-54dc-93e7-68a2d21650fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527456} {:answer/id #uuid "7bbe6e05-0499-5983-af56-20633ca4dbda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527540} {:answer/id #uuid "a7952181-9829-5c46-9aa2-b5542796cd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527652} {:answer/id #uuid "d455ccfa-c0ef-50c1-9901-ee6c36ee313c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a3ab933-6930-5f67-8ca1-c0039736f563" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527401} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f093291-4e87-5afd-b4d2-1d112101a7e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc25546e-e94f-545f-9768-cf226be3dc76" :question/math-academy-id "q-15939" :question/problem "Find the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,1]$ given the following table of values for $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,-3\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the averge rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1)-f(-3)}{1-(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-2}{1-(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f7224e3-9c13-51e7-a3f7-0e379f63a861" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change Given a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "254ff639-49a7-5804-99ec-040b9ef96440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527390} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4a206e-e770-563b-b20f-5959d1004976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527454} {:answer/id #uuid "91c81b1e-e7fe-58fd-a39e-76fc375fb786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527593} {:answer/id #uuid "a92b0a77-fd8a-5040-b3c0-93eeef68bf39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527655} {:answer/id #uuid "e73b4c6a-cd5c-55d9-93bd-aeeb22c59c0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "254ff639-49a7-5804-99ec-040b9ef96440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527390} :answer-field/id #uuid "a857d99b-4347-5fe1-ae63-d9fb653c5ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc7ad0f1-6b84-5b13-8e8e-b050839dc127" :question/math-academy-id "q-19157" :question/problem "The table below lists values of $f(x)$ at distinct $x$-values. Knowing that the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[2p,2]$ is $3,$ find the value of $p.$ \n\n| $x$ | $\\,-9\\,$ | $\\,-4\\,$ | $\\,2p\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,-12\\,$ | $\\,-8\\,$ | $\\,-4\\,$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ | $\\,8\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2)-f(2p)}{2-2p} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-(-4)}{2-2p} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{2-2p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we know that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=3$ on the interval $[2p,2].$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{2-2p}=3.\n$$\n\nSolving for $p,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{2-2p} & =3 \\\\ 12 & =3\\cdot (2-2p) \\\\ 12 & =6-6p \\\\ 12-6 & =-6p \\\\ 6 & =-6p \\\\ \\frac{6}{-6} & =\\frac{-6p}{-6} \\\\ -1 & =p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $p=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064267 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68635d27-a9ef-541b-a57b-d9f5f422ae85" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb2e6d9-a77d-57a2-9067-88938b25fdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061586} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c43b9e-95bc-527c-aaa8-97ef8fe71eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061587} {:answer/id #uuid "eab80576-cf3c-565b-8b70-625ee7c85497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061588} {:answer/id #uuid "ecdbf5c9-b46e-558c-a271-c8dd2bf11f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061589} {:answer/id #uuid "1bdd418b-40e8-5c8b-9aee-f67c99347494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9c43b9e-95bc-527c-aaa8-97ef8fe71eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061587} :answer-field/id #uuid "258c7721-283b-58d1-a5c6-b9d2648fb034" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e460d45e-d406-504b-ba46-cb34526931e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-20832" :question/problem "A curve is defined as $y={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3x.$ Find the average rate of change of $y$ over the interval $[-1,3].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3x.$ Applying the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-1)}{3-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{[{3}^{4}-3({3}^{3})+3(3)]-[(-1)^{4}-3(-1)^{3}+3(-1)]}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d13310c-2b80-5945-ada3-31d886f1ec48" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27306d36-45a1-5604-894a-5eadba2655cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527397} {:answer/id #uuid "29d010d4-e5b1-5059-b751-2f4a771e669a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527400} {:answer/id #uuid "3009e8c1-cc42-545c-bb17-c691f82ab15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527408} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e9c8a0-9fe7-5ead-9499-3748062210ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527678} {:answer/id #uuid "dd824001-dc88-5caf-96af-b744606daaf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$16$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27306d36-45a1-5604-894a-5eadba2655cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527397} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f104ee8-87d5-5203-8242-d7623b593716" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6dc0dd6-8281-5909-b3f4-b0dcdc2e7ecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-21120" :question/problem "The height $h(t),$ measured in feet, of a plant after $t$ years is given by the expression $h(t)=3{t}^{3/2}-2t.$ What is the average rate of growth over the first $4$ years?" :question/worked-solution "Let $h(t)=3{t}^{3/2}-2t,$ the height measured in feet, of a plant after $t$ years. To find the average rate of change of $h(t)$ from $t=0$ to $t=4,$ we use the average rate of change formula on the interval $[0,4]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δh}{Δt} & =\\frac{h(b)-h(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{h(4)-h(0)}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3({4}^{3/2})-2(4)]-[3({0}^{3/2})-2(0)]}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-8}{4} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average rate of growth is $4$ feet per year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d13310c-2b80-5945-ada3-31d886f1ec48" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b80882e-b1e3-564a-a8a5-498ba9503c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.1$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527331} {:answer/id #uuid "364e5a27-2868-5fed-9db3-b66939ad6bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527419} {:answer/id #uuid "63933aae-7d36-5a04-8110-7d43fcb6353e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.3$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527496} {:answer/id #uuid "7e13ffe8-87de-5b95-ae86-d026dd0c130e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.2$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527547} {:answer/id #uuid "9e45c463-2092-56da-8831-7117a8290302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b80882e-b1e3-564a-a8a5-498ba9503c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.1$ feet per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527331} :answer-field/id #uuid "146f8099-e4d4-5cdd-b5f2-ef7311761518" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c25ff0b-f786-5f82-b2d5-6e5163b97efc" :question/math-academy-id "q-21129" :question/problem "The ice level in the North Pole is decreasing due to global warming. The thickness of ice, measured in feet, in the North Pole, is represented by the expression $135+0.1x-0.02{x}^{2},$ where $x$ is the time, in years, since measurements began. What is the average rate of decrease of the ice thickness over the first $10$ years?" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=135+0.1x-0.02{x}^{2}$ be the thickness of the ice, in feet, after $x$ years. To find the average rate of change of the ice thickness over the first $10$ years, we use the average rate of change formula on the interval $[0,10]$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(10)-f(0)}{10-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{[135+0.1(10)-0.02(10)^{2}]-[135+0.1(0)-0.02(0)^{2}]}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{134-135}{10} \\\\  & =-0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average rate of decrease of the ice thickness over the first $10$ years is $0.1$ feet per year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064267 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68635d27-a9ef-541b-a57b-d9f5f422ae85" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31fc5c7c-2c99-595a-be35-1730c9c6d670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31fc5c7c-2c99-595a-be35-1730c9c6d670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527412} :answer-field/id #uuid "04d5c705-53d2-5991-aabc-2e06b5e9777c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5381d86b-69c1-53d6-ab4d-bc350eeb1469" :question/math-academy-id "q-218679" :question/problem "![](images/38/386b2307d81c8f0aa895a192ac2734a7b24f122edb26229f3f9c10f0941c96e7.png)\n\nThe average rate of change of the curve shown above, over the interval $[0,4]$, is $\\frac{Δy}{Δx}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we can see that $f(0)=-2$ and $f(4)=1.$\n\nApplying the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4)-f(0)}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-2)}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064267 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68635d27-a9ef-541b-a57b-d9f5f422ae85" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Rate of Change of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f878120-87ed-5ef6-bb55-635561a914cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527338} {:answer/id #uuid "195ced6a-50f6-5fb3-96af-0a4ed9c5bd51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527362} {:answer/id #uuid "1c36149f-d257-541c-af17-0a3cfef20f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527370} {:answer/id #uuid "578b641f-9374-51cf-a20b-16caea5f4a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527474} {:answer/id #uuid "ef71486c-efc5-509d-b5e4-7307352e1c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "578b641f-9374-51cf-a20b-16caea5f4a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527474} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f068c8-83d6-567f-8453-a2683cd9c143" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dba8d021-2c20-52de-b1fb-abd8fe5f7a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-2448" :question/problem "A curve is defined as $y=3x-5.$ Find the average rate of change of $y$ over the interval $[3,7].$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3x-5.$ Applying the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(7)-f(3)}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3(7)-5]-[3(3)-5]]}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16-4}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051b5337-7671-599f-a7f3-c3fb064575cc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Interval Over Which the Average Rate of Change is Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24580eb6-e1cf-5ab7-aa36-5ecedfce4d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,7]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527388} {:answer/id #uuid "7382e664-e01c-56c8-a5e9-17c73c3682e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527524} {:answer/id #uuid "968058f5-e63c-524f-b4e2-f7e0efe6f67e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527608} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c7638e-969c-5f74-899c-3dc7992e09f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3,7]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527781} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c0f760-5c10-5dac-a1c4-dcaf32da92de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-1,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7382e664-e01c-56c8-a5e9-17c73c3682e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527524} :answer-field/id #uuid "199d7d79-b9a3-56a1-aa69-1dc32f5615f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8be6849-5f2a-595e-8c72-25b5d6a335d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-69666" :question/problem "Find the interval where the average rate of change of $f(x)$ equals $0$ given the following table of values of $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,5\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,-5\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,-4\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ if and only if $Δf=0.$ So\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & Δf=0 \\\\  & f(b)-f(a)=0 \\\\  & f(b)=f(a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means we have to find an interval  $[a,b]$ such that $f(a)=f(b).$\n\nSince $f(-1)=f(5)=3,$ we conclude that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ on the interval $[-1,5].$"}]}
